    "question_id": "Q1.9",
    "class": 11,
    "subject": "business_studies",
    "chapter_number": 1,
    "chapter_name": "nature and purpose of business",
    "question_type": "conceptual",
    "question_text": "What is business risk? What is its nature?",
    "question_latex": null,
    "mcq_options": [],
    "correct_option": null,
    "question_image": {
      "present": false,
      "description": null,
      "cloudinary_url": null,
      "latex_extracted": null,
      "source_page_number": null,
      "source_image_index": null,
      "ownership": "unknown"
    },
    "parts": [],
    "answer_text": "Business risk is the possibility of failing to earn sufficient profits or incurring losses as a result of various unforeseen circumstances which are beyond the control of a business. The nature of business risk includes: Business risks arise due to uncertainties, Risk is an essential part of every business, Degree of risk depends mainly upon the nature and size of business, Profit is the reward for risk taking. Business risks arise due to a variety of causes including natural, human, economic and other causes.",
    "answer_latex": null,
    "steps": [],
    "final_answer": "Therefore, understanding business risk is crucial for effective management.",
