      "source_image_index": null,
      "ownership": "unknown"
    },
    "parts": [],
    "answer_text": "Basis Business Profession Employment\nMode of establishment Entrepreneur’s decision and a professional letter and other legal formalities, if necessary.\nNature of work Provision of goods and personalized, expert services.\nQualification No minimum qualification is necessary. Expertise and training in a specific field is must.\nReward or return Profit earned. Professional fee. Salary or wages.\nCapital Capital investment required as per size and nature of business. Limited capital investment needed for establishment.\nRisk Profits are uncertain and irregular; risk is present. Fee is generally fixed and regular; no risk.\nTransfer of interest Transfer possible with some formalities. Not possible.\nCode of conduct No code of conduct is prescribed. Professional code of behavior laid down by the employer are to be followed.",
    "answer_latex": null,
