  {
    "question_id": "Q1.12",
    "class": 11,
    "subject": "business_studies",
    "chapter_number": 1,
    "chapter_name": "nature and purpose of business",
    "question_type": "conceptual",
    "question_text": "Explain with examples the various types of industries.",
    "question_latex": null,
    "mcq_options": [],
    "correct_option": null,
    "question_image": {
      "present": false,
      "description": null,
      "cloudinary_url": null,
      "latex_extracted": null,
      "source_page_number": null,
      "source_image_index": null,
      "ownership": "unknown"
    },
    "parts": [],
    "answer_text": "The various types of industries are:\n→ Primary Industries: These industries directly use natural resources as their raw materials and convert them into a consumable form such as Agriculture, mining, fishing, etc. These can be sub divided as\n• Extractive industries: These industries supply some basic raw materials that are mostly products of geographical or natural environment, which further process these products into useful goods. Example: Agriculture, fisheries, mining, etc.\n• Genetic industries: These industries remain engaged in breeding plants and animals for their use in further reproduction. Example: Seeds and nursery industries and poultry farming.\n→ Secondary industries: These industries use raw material from primary industries to produce goods for final consumption or for further processing by other industrial units. For example, mining of an iron ore is a primary industry, but manufacturing of steel by way of further processing of raw irons is a secondary industry.\n• Manufacturing industries: These industries are engaged in producing goods through processing of raw materials and thus creating form utilities. These can be further divided into:\n(i) Analytical industry which analyses and separates different elements from the same materials, as in the case of oil refinery.\n(ii) Synthetical industry which combines various ingredients into a new product, as in the case of cement.\n(iii) Processing industry which involves successive stages for manufacturing finished products, as in the case of sugar and paper.\n(iv) Assembling industry which assembles different component parts to make a new product, as in the case of television, car, computer, etc.\n• Construction industries: These industries are involved in the construction of buildings, dams, bridges, roads as well as tunnels and canals.\n→ Tertiary Industries: These are concerned with providing support services to the public.",
    "answer_latex": null,
    "steps": [],
    "final_answer": "Industries can be classified into primary, secondary, and tertiary, each serving different roles in the economy.",
    "answer_image": {
      "present": false,
      "description": null,
      "cloudinary_url": null,
      "latex_extracted": null,
      "source_page_number": null,
      "source_image_index": null,
      "ownership": "unknown"
    },
    "difficulty_rating": 3,
    "difficulty_reasoning": "Requires understanding of different industry types and their examples.",
